course: dictionary
lesson: 2934
title: Dread: fear of what is coming
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dread can be a verb, a noun or an adjective. As a verb, it means to feel very worried or afraid about something that is going to happen. «Ben dreads going to the dentist.» The dentist has not happened yet, so the fear is about the future.
explain: As a noun, dread is a strong feeling of fear about what is coming. «She was filled with dread as the test began.» The clue words filled and fear show it is a bad, heavy feeling, not a happy one.
explain: In old or literary stories, dread can be an adjective meaning causing great fear, as in «the dread pirate». Check your meaning by swapping in a word like fearful. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Dread is a verb, a noun and an adjective.
fact: As a verb, «dread» means to feel very worried or afraid about something that is going to happen.
fact: As a noun, «dread» means a strong feeling of fear about the future.
fact: «I dread to think» means you are too worried to even imagine what might have happened.
fact: Informally, «dreads» is short for dreadlocks, a hairstyle of long twisted strands.
exercise: «She was filled with dread as the test began.» What does dread mean here? | *A strong feeling of fear about what is coming | A happy feeling of excitement | A loud noise | A sleepy, calm feeling
exercise: In «Ben dreads going to the dentist», which word is the verb? | *dreads | Ben | dentist | going to
exercise: «The dread pirate sailed into the harbour.» In this sentence, dread means: | *Causing great fear | Very kind | Lost at sea | Very tired
test: «Ethan dreads Monday mornings.» Here dreads means: | Looks forward to with joy | Plays happily | Forgets quickly | *Feels worried about something that is going to happen
test: The phrase «I dread to think» means: | I am glad to think | I am thinking very hard | I am bored of thinking | *I am too worried to even imagine it
exam: Which word means nearly the same as dreaded in «A girl in London dreaded school»? | *Feared | Ignored | Looked forward to | Enjoyed
